.TH CONSOLE-CAPTURE 1 "2026" "1.0.0" "Network Utilities"
.SH NAME
console-capture \- capture Cisco CLI output over a serial console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B console-capture
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR \fIBAUD\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIUSERNAME\fR]
[\fB\-P\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fICMD\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B console-capture
connects to a Cisco network device via a serial console cable, sends CLI
commands, and writes the captured output to a timestamped text file named
after the device hostname.
.PP
By default the commands
.B show run brief
and
.B show interfaces status
are sent.  Use
.B \-c
to replace them with your own commands.
.PP
Serial ports are auto-detected using
.BR udev (7)
if \fB\-\-port\fR is not specified.  The tool handles username/password login
prompts and automatically disables terminal pagination (\fIterminal length 0\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPATH\fR
Serial device path (e.g.\& \fI/dev/ttyUSB0\fR).
If omitted, available TTY devices are discovered via udev and the user is
prompted to choose one.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-baud " " \fIRATE\fR
Baud rate for the serial connection (default: \fB9600\fR).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " " \fIUSER\fR
Login username.  Prompted interactively if the device requires credentials
and this option is not supplied.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASS\fR
Login password.  Prompted securely via \fBgetpass\fR if required and not
supplied on the command line.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Path for the output text file.
Default: \fI<hostname>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt\fR in the current directory,
where \fI<hostname>\fR is read from the device prompt after login.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICMD\fR
CLI command to send to the device.  May be repeated to run multiple commands.
Replaces the default command list when supplied.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Auto-detect port, interactive login, auto-named output file:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
console-capture
.EE
.RE
.PP
Specify port and username:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
console-capture -p /dev/ttyUSB0 -u admin
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run custom commands instead of the defaults:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
console-capture -c "show version" -c "show ip route"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Save to a specific file:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
console-capture -p /dev/ttyUSB0 -o capture.txt
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cisco-console-capture/
Python virtual environment containing the tool and its dependencies.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/console-capture
Wrapper shell script that invokes the tool from the virtual environment.
.SH NOTES
The user running this command must be a member of the
.B dialout
group to access serial devices without root privileges:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo usermod -aG dialout $USER
.EE
.RE
.PP
Log out and back in after adding yourself to the group.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux only (udev is required).  Python 3.10 or newer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR screen (1),
.BR minicom (1),
.BR udev (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Cisco Console Capture 1.0.0
